 to get you meal popping let's  start with the first step take baby  steps you don't have to prep all your  meals start with one single meal for  instance you can choose to prep your  lunch to take it up with you I suggest  starting with single recipe meals  instead of making meals that require two  to three recipes which can be very  complicated make a one-pot dish that  contains protein cups and vegetables and  start with recipes that you already know  this will give you more confidence in  what you're cooking that's how I got  started I used to make baked fish with  vegetables and eventually I started to  experiment with different recipes you  can check out all my recipe videos on my  channel I believe in keeping things  simple because I know that everybody can  cook remember take baby steps don't try  to do too much and overwhelm yourself so  start with one meal and eventually add  another meal the next step is to know  your ingredients and cooking methods  when it comes to meal prepping and  wanting your nails to keep well for at  least up to four days choose ingredients  that will not produce much liquid when  cooked and can be kept and reheated  without losing much of their texture so  let's start with vegetables some really  great vegetables include carrot broccoli  pumpkin potatoes bell pepper whole  cherry tomatoes cauliflower leafy greens  such as lettuce or spinach rockets and  killed basically foods that will not  produce too much liquid after cooking  and can be kept for days say that  however you can still cook your  vegetables and blend them up to make  vegetable soups which can be frozen and  will last for many weeks and simply  reheat one portion at a time next  protein pretty much all protein are  suitable such as chicken beef fish eggs  tempeh tofu beans or pulses this really  comes down to the cooking method in  order for them to last long fully cook  your protein so make scrambled eggs or a  hard boil eggs and keep them with a  shell on rather 